      "end": 562,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Apollo Victoria Theatre\nThe Apollo Victoria Theatre is a West End theatre on Wilton Road in the Westminster district of London , across from London Victoria Station . ( The theatre also has an entrance on Vauxhall Bridge Road . ) Opened in 1930 as a cinema and variety theatre , the Apollo Victoria became a venue for musical theatre , beginning with The Sound of Music in 1981 , and including the long-running Starlight Express , from 1984 to 2002 . The theatre is now the home of the musical Wicked , which has played for eleven years at the venue as of 2017 ."
